  "body": "Peak-memory optimization on top of stable f9ac027.\n\n- cap concurrently WORKING CATALOG_SCAN jobs at 3 by default\n- keep worker count and RUNNING bot count unchanged\n- defer excess catalog jobs back into the scheduler instead of blocking worker threads\n- allow NEGOTIATION_CHECK / PRICE_PROBE to remain eligible while catalog capacity is full\n- expose FLIPBOT_MAX_CONCURRENT_CATALOG_SCANS (1..100); set 10 to approximate the old behavior\n- add scheduler tests proving excess catalogs defer and negotiations are not starved\n\nNo BrowserManager, session, negotiation decision, quota, backend or frontend code is changed.",
